{
  "seed": "bigville_trade",
  "version": "2.2.0",
  "comment": "TRADE IS TWO ACTIONS. A buyer PROPOSES an Offer to a seller (from its expectation of who has the good -- bc_do_acquire); the SELLER decides to accept (tr_accept), decline (tr_decline), or -- if it hasn't the good -- the buyer is SURPRISED and its expectation weakens (tr_surprise). Expectation-driven, co-location NOT required: you can ask the baker in the street. Two parties, two decisions. A trade is CO-LOCATED (buyer + seller at the same cell) -- the agents run on the map; you go to whom you trade with. A sale needs a present, conscious, willing person co-located with the buyer. Opening hours are a CONSTRUCT (the seller's routine), NOT an engine gate -- the baker 'shut' means gone home / asleep, so the buyer finds no one to deal with.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "tr_accept",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "Trade action 2 of 2 -- the SELLER'S DECISION: an Offer is made to this seller for a good it HOLDS (has_good, qty>=1), the buyer can pay the seller's price, and the seller is willing -> it SELLS: coin<->good transfer, offer accepted. The seller can decline (tr_decline). Co-location NOT required -- you can sell to someone who asked you in the street. The buyer's proposal is a separate action (bc_do_acquire). Trade is two decisions by two parties, not one. CO-LOCATED: buyer and seller must be at the SAME place -- you trade with a person where they are (you go to them). Not the shop building; the person's location. The seller must be a PRESENT, CONSCIOUS person (not asleep/collapsed) -- a sale is done by a person who is there and awake. OPENING HOURS ARE A CONSTRUCT (the seller's routine of being at the shop by day, home asleep by night), not an engine gate.",
